    {
      "id": "xsz5lsa",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Industry"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Industries process raw materials into finished goods, forming the backbone of the secondary economic sector.",
        "Industries are broadly classified by raw materials (agro, mineral, forest-based), size (small vs. large scale), and ownership (public, private, joint, cooperative).",
        "Major industrial clusters in India include Mumbai-Pune, Hugli, Bengaluru-Tamil Nadu, and Chota Nagpur regions.",
        "Industrial site location depends heavily on geographical factors like raw material proximity, water, and power, as well as non-geographical factors like capital and transport.",
        "India's industrial policies evolved from public sector dominance (1956 Policy) to market-driven reforms under the 1991 LPG policy."
      ],
      "id": "rot0d98"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3r0bu1o",
      "content": "• Industry refers to economic activities related to the production of goods."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bl3z8vk",
      "content": "• It involves the conversion of raw materials into finished products."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tmw6fgv",
      "content": "• Industries help in increasing production and economic growth."
    },
    {
