      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Factors Affecting Industrial Location"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vq8lmsu",
      "content": "• Availability of raw materials."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ozm88sa",
      "content": "• Availability of labour."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s2gij8v",
      "content": "• Availability of power supply."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Agro-Based Industry",
        "Mineral-Based Industry"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Uses plant and animal-based agricultural products as raw materials",
          "Uses mineral ores and metals as raw materials"
        ],
        [
          "Examples: Cotton Textiles, Sugar, Jute, Edible Oil",
          "Examples: Iron and Steel, Cement, Aluminum, Heavy Machinery"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "vlxm3xb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pdou49a",
      "content": "• Transportation facilities."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jy6y79j",
      "content": "• Market availability."
    },
    {
      "id": "wcjufkd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Industrial Policies in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wlmmfo9",
      "content": "• Industrial Policy Resolution 1948 – first industrial policy of India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bo4m6f3",
      "content": "• Industrial Policy Resolution 1956 – emphasized public sector development."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qdrei5p",
      "content": "• New Industrial Policy 1991 – liberalization, privatization and globalization."
    },
    {
      "id": "7y8ccus",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Importance of Industries"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ygyhu3p",
      "content": "• Generates employment opportunities."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5nvveke",
      "content": "• Increases national income."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The Industrial Policy Resolution of 1956 is frequently referred to as the 'Economic Constitution of India'.",
        "Chota Nagpur region is commonly termed the 'Ruhr of India' due to its vast mineral wealth and heavy steel industries.",
        "The New Industrial Policy of 1991 introduced Liberalization, Privatization, and Globalization (LPG)."
      ],
      "id": "wp2nqrj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "amjqarw",
      "content": "• Promotes technological advancement."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0euhdlp",
      "content": "• Supports export growth."
    },
    {
      "id": "3r6fuyy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zup00wc",
      "content": "• Jamshedpur is famous for iron and steel industry."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kirf5si",
      "content": "• Mumbai is known as the cotton textile capital of India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "it4fcpx",
      "content": "• Chota Nagpur Plateau is the main industrial region due to mineral resources."
    }
